      "content": "Those are good starting points. The \"communion of rights\" angle is particularly sharp for a high school level. \n\nTo make sure they're fully prepared for the round, could you expand on the \"national security\" aspect? I want them to be able to argue that border security isn't just about economics or law, but a fundamental necessity for maintaining a stable state. Give me some sophisticated phrasing they can use to link border control directly to the prevention of internal societal collapse or the protection of democratic institutions.",
